{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מוצאי", :translit "motza'i", :gloss "my emerging"} {:he "כי מוצאי מצא חיים", :translit "ki motza'i matza chayim", :gloss "for whoever finds me has found life"} {:he "סמא דחיי", :translit "sama de-chayei", :gloss "elixir of life"} {:he "סמא דמותא", :translit "sama de-mota", :gloss "elixir of death"} {:he "והיה כל מוצאי יהרגני", :translit "vehaya kol motza'i yahargeni", :gloss "and it shall be that whoever finds me will kill me"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מוצאי" "כי מוצאי מצא חיים"]} {:kind :other, :note "A word serving as elixir of life in one verse context becomes elixir of death in another."}], :frame {:text "The Sages taught: whoever engages in Torah, if he is worthy it becomes for him an elixir of life, and if not, an elixir of death (Yoma 72b). A related teaching: this one interpreted it to the right and it became for him an elixir of life, this one to the left and it became for him an elixir of death (Shabbat 88a). Ba'al HaTurim applies this to the word מוצאי: in Proverbs 8:35 the same root yields life — כי מוצאי מצא חיים — but here in Genesis 4:14 it yields death — והיה כל מוצאי יהרגני.", :sources ["Yoma 72b" "Shabbat 88a" "Proverbs 8:35" "Genesis 4:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מוצאי" "כי מוצאי מצא חיים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מוצאי", :refs ["Numbers 14:37" "Ezekiel 44:5" "Psalms 65:9"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי מוצאי מצא חיים", :refs ["Proverbs 8:35"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "A word serving as elixir of life in one verse context becomes elixir of death in another.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:33.773010577Z", :model "glm-5.2"}